+### `rotate(steps = 1)` -> `Denque`
+
+Rotate this queue in place and return the same queue instance. Positive steps
+move values from the back to the front; negative steps move values from the
+front to the back. Finite integer step counts are normalized modulo the queue
+length. A zero rotation, or a rotation of an empty or singleton queue, does
+not change the queue. Non-integer, non-finite, and non-number step counts throw
+an `Error`.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1,2,3,4]);
+denque.rotate();
+denque.toArray(); // [4,1,2,3]
+denque.rotate(-2);
+denque.toArray(); // [2,3,4,1]
+```
+
+
+
 ### `pop()` -> `dynamic`
 
 Pop off the item at the back of this queue.
